+## On DeepSeek Harness, read this first
+
+Everything below describes a Markdown sheet (`<config-home>/pstack-models.md`) plus a parent integration line in `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md`. **DSH uses neither.** On DSH the sheet is a JSON overlay at `$DSH_HOME/pstack-dsh.json`, and steps 7 and 8 are replaced by the four paragraphs here. Steps 1 through 6 still apply unchanged as the *choice* logic: pick one requested effort per family, decide which roles leave `inherit-parent`.
+
+**Where the sheet lives.** `$DSH_HOME/pstack-dsh.json`, shape `{ version: 1, roles: { <role>: { inherit: true, routes: [] } } }`. `inherit: true` with empty routes means the role runs on the parent conversation's route. A non-empty `routes` array is a list of `{ provider, model, effort }`; a panel role has more than one entry and `route_index` selects the lane. Do not create a second config file and do not write `~/.cursor/rules`, `~/.claude/rules`, or a `pstack-models.md`.
+
+**How to write it.** Two ways, same file. A human clicks **Settings → pstack** in the DSH Web UI. An agent calls `pstack_overlay_write` with the complete overlay object; it validates every provider, model, and effort against live routes before saving and rejects the whole write otherwise. Never hand-edit the JSON to add a route you have not validated, and never write it while a spawn is in flight.
+
+**Validate against the live harness, not a vendor list.** `pstack_catalog` is the only source of routes that actually run on this machine: registered adapters holding a logged-in key, plus OAuth store routes. It also reports each model's real `reasoning.efforts`. A descriptor whose effort id is absent from that model's list is rejected at call time, so check it before writing. Upstream's `grok:grok-4.7@xhigh`, `codex:gpt-6.1-sol@max`, and `claude:opus@max` are Cursor's routes. Do not copy them onto DSH; map each family onto a route this machine has, and say plainly when a family has no local equivalent instead of inventing a slug.
+
+**A read-only catalog is not data loss.** `pstack_catalog` can report `routes: []` while `$DSH_HOME/pstack-dsh.json` still holds a full role map, because the catalog reads harness registrations while spawn reads the overlay. Treat an empty catalog as "the picker cannot offer choices right now". Do **not** press Save or write the overlay to "fix" it: saving a rendered empty catalog overwrites every role with inherit. Read the overlay file directly to report what is configured, and tell the operator the picker is degraded rather than editing around it.
+
+**Smoke test.** One `pstack_spawn` per configured role with `run_in_background: false` and a prompt that returns a unique marker. The returned text proves the overlay route resolved; the spawn result also reports `inherit: false`, which distinguishes a real route from a parent fallback. Steps 10 and 11 (offering verification and formal-verification skills) apply on DSH unchanged, except the generated skill lands under `$DSH_HOME/skills/verify-<app>/` rather than `.claude/skills/`.
 
